Experiment: Port Scanning and Information Gathering Using Nmap
Aim
To perform port scanning and information gathering using Nmap and identify open, closed, and filtered ports on an authorized target system.

Tool Required
Nmap (Network Mapper)
Windows/Linux System
Command Prompt / Terminal
Authorized Target System
Core Concepts
Nmap is a network scanning tool used to discover hosts, identify open ports, detect running services, and gather basic information about a network or system.

Port States
Open: A service is actively listening on the port.
Closed: The port is reachable, but no service is listening.
Filtered: Nmap cannot determine whether the port is open because a firewall or filtering device is blocking the scan.
Procedure and Commands
Step 1: Check Nmap Installation
nmap --version
Step 2: Perform a Basic Scan
nmap 127.0.0.1
This performs a basic scan of the local system.

Step 3: Scan Specific Ports
nmap -p 22,80,443 127.0.0.1
This scans ports 22, 80, and 443.

Step 4: Scan a Port Range
nmap -p 1-1000 127.0.0.1
This scans ports from 1 to 1000.

Step 5: Service and Version Detection
nmap -sV 127.0.0.1
This attempts to identify the services and their versions running on open ports.

Step 6: Operating System Detection
nmap -O 127.0.0.1
This attempts to identify the operating system of the target.

Step 7: Save Scan Results
nmap -sV 127.0.0.1 -oN scan_results.txt
This saves the scan results in a text file.

Steps
Install Nmap on the system.
Open Command Prompt or Terminal.
Select an authorized target system.
Check whether Nmap is installed using the nmap --version command.
Perform a basic port scan.
Identify open, closed, and filtered ports.
Perform service and version detection using -sV.
Perform OS detection using -O.
Save the scan results for documentation.
Analyze the information obtained from the scan.
Sample Output
PORT    STATE    SERVICE
22/tcp  open     ssh
80/tcp  open     http
443/tcp open     https
The output may vary depending on the target system.

Conclusion
Nmap was successfully used to perform basic port scanning and information gathering. The experiment demonstrated how to identify port states and gather information about services running on an authorized system. Nmap is useful for network administration, security auditing, and identifying exposed services.

Safety Note
Nmap should only be used on systems that you own or have explicit permission to scan.
